They have no third-party code in them. There is no vendored library, no minified bundle,
no framework and no webfont anywhere in this repository. Everything under those paths was
written for it.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. The written content — all rights reserved
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
content/ and docs/ are NOT covered by the MIT License above.

They are the author's own writing about the author's own projects: what was built, why one
approach was chosen over another, and what was tried and abandoned. They are published to
be read and cited, not to be reused as text.

  - Quoting a passage with attribution and a link: fine, and welcome.
  - Republishing pages, in whole or in bulk, as your own or as a dataset: not granted.

content/ is generated. Its source of truth is a private repository; every file in it opens
with a banner saying so, and the build refuses to run if one has been edited here.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. What the pages describe, and what they do not disclose
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The pages name fifteen repositories the author built, and quote files inside them. Those
repositories are separate works with their own licences and their own NOTICE files where
one applies. A quotation here does not relicense the file it came from.

Three of the source repositories contain coursework in security, business systems and a
forensic data investigation. Pages resting on those repositories were each read and
cleared individually before publication, and are recorded as cleared in the private
repository's configuration rather than waved through. Naming a repository as one of the
places a pattern was confirmed discloses no material from it.

Nothing published here contains credentials, keys, tokens, personal data, institutional
identifiers, student numbers, or the names of collaborators. Collaborators are referred to
by role. An automated scan for secret-shaped strings runs over the content bundle before
it is written and again in continuous integration, and a match stops the build.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. Accuracy
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Every page states the files it was written from. Where a reason could not be established
from a repository or from the author, the page says so and is marked low confidence — no
plausible-sounding explanation was ever invented to fill a gap, because an invented reason
is indistinguishable from a real one later.

The figures on the site measure coverage, retrieval and process. They do not certify that
any claim on any page is correct.
